  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "The APEC jackets were intended to reflect \"both traditional Chinese flavor and modern ideals\". They have straight Mandarin collars, similar to those on the changshan and magua that gave the style its name. Unlike the traditional 2D \"flat-cutting\" (平面裁剪, píngmiàn cáijiǎn) process used to create those garments, which tends to produce a baggy and ill-fitted look, tangzhuangs are made using the 3D \"solid-cutting\" (t 立體裁剪, s 立体裁剪, lìtǐ cáijiǎn) process developed in Europe."
  },
